# Trivy vulnerability allowlist.
#
# Add an entry only after triaging the CVE. Every line is either:
#   - a CVE ID that exists in a fixed upstream version we have not yet
#     bumped to (tracked for the next dependency-bump PR), or
#   - an OS-level CVE whose fix is not yet in the base image and whose
#     runtime exposure is limited by the container surface.
#
# Review this list quarterly. Remove entries as soon as the upstream
# fix lands in either the Python deps or the base image.

# ── Python deps (also listed in the pip-audit --ignore-vuln flags in
#    .github/workflows/ci.yml; keep the two lists in sync until the
#    dependency-bump PR raises cryptography>=46.0.6 and pyopenssl>=26).
CVE-2026-26007  # cryptography <46.0.5 — fixed upstream, pending bump
CVE-2026-34073  # cryptography <46.0.6 name-constraint bypass
CVE-2026-25990  # pillow <12.1.1 PSD OOB write
CVE-2026-40192  # pillow <12.2.0 FITS decompression bomb
CVE-2026-27448  # pyopenssl <26.0.0 SNI callback bypass
CVE-2026-27459  # pyopenssl <26.0.0 cookie-cb buffer overflow
CVE-2025-71176  # pytest <9.0.3 /tmp race (dev-only, low risk)

# ── Base-image OS CVEs (Debian bookworm slim, tracked for base-image
#    bump). All are DoS or local-privilege escalations that require
#    attacker code inside the container; the container runs as non-root
#    and the app does not spawn shells or parse untrusted systemd / ncurses
#    input at runtime.
CVE-2026-28390  # openssl / libssl3 DoS — fixed in 3.5.5-1~deb13u2
CVE-2026-29111  # systemd / libsystemd / libudev arbitrary code — deb13 pending
CVE-2026-27135  # libnghttp2 HTTP/2 DoS — deb13 pending
CVE-2025-69720  # ncurses / libtinfo buffer overflow — deb13 pending
